DXVK 3.1.1 d3d11: CreateDirect3D11DeviceFromDXGIDevice and CreateDirect3D11SurfaceFromDXGISurface.

Windows' d3d11.dll exports both: they wrap a DXGI device or surface as a WinRT IDirect3DDevice / IDirect3DSurface that
hands the DXGI object back through IDirect3DDxgiInterfaceAccess. Lightroom Classic's video_toolkit.dll imports
CreateDirect3D11SurfaceFromDXGISurface for the What's New videos (MediaPlayer.CopyFrameToVideoSurface takes such a
surface); DXVK did not export it. Test: LinDobe's wine/tests/mf/mfwinrt.c uses it when d3d11.dll exports it.

